  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: db176a60e3b58b4408636b22a97519c4, type: 3}
  m_Name: DustStormEvent
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MarsEvent
  eventTitle: Dust Storm
  eventDescription: A massive dust storm is approaching the Mars outpost. Dust accumulation
    is reducing the efficiency of the solar panels, threatening the base's energy
    supply. You must decide how to manage the situation while keeping the crew safe.
  targetSol: 3
  optionATitle: Clean Solar Panels
  energyChangeA: -8
  lifeSupportChangeA: 0
  shieldChangeA: 0
  resultTitleA: Solar Panels Cleaned
  resultDescriptionA: The crew successfully removes dust from the solar panels during
    a safe maintenance window. The operation consumes energy, but helps maintain
    the base's solar power system. Copy
  optionBTitle: Reduce Power Consumption
  energyChangeB: 5
  lifeSupportChangeB: -8
  shieldChangeB: 0
  resultTitleB: Power Conservation Activated
  resultDescriptionB: The crew reduces electricity consumption by limiting nonessential
    systems. Energy reserves improve, but reduced environmental support places additional
    strain on the habitat's life support resources.
  educationalExplanation: Mars frequently experiences dust storms that can last for
    days or even weeks. Airborne dust reduces the sunlight reaching solar panels,
    while accumulated dust can further decrease their efficiency. This makes energy
    management an important challenge for solar-powered missions on Mars. Copy explanation
  scientificSource: "NASA \u2014 Mars Exploration"
  scientificSourceURL: https://science.nasa.gov/mars/
